<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλί̄τ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπλον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>heavy-armed, armed,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. δρόμοι</span> races <i>of men in
				armour,</i> opp. the naked race (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				1.23
			</span></i> ; called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ὁ.</span> or simply
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλίτης</span> (
				Dor.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τας</span>) in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1120
			</span></i> (Geronthrae, <span class="entity">v B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				5(2).550.26
			</span></i> (Lycaeum, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), etc. (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ὅπλου δρόμος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				6.13.1
			</span></i>), cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλιτοδρομέω</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ ὁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					717
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				585
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. στρατός</span>
			<i>an armed</i> host, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				800
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. κόσμος</span>
			<i>warrior</i>-dress, armour, ib.<i><span class="en">
				699
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> mostly as
				Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλίτης, ὁ,</span>
			<i>heavy-armed foot-soldier, man-at-arms,</i> who carried a pike
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόρυ</span>) and a large shield (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπλον</span>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηναίων οἱ στρατηγοὶ καὶ . . οἱ ὁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12.116.25
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλῖται,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιλοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.106
			</span></i> ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυμνῆτες,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.63
			</span></i> ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππεῖς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				552a
			</span></i> ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξόται,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				119b
			</span></i> ; to be a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλίτης</span> implied
			the possession of full civic rights, hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ
				ὁ.,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ βάναυσοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1326a23
			</span></i> ; and, in oligarchical states, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
				δῆμος,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1305b33
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
